The two favorites won their heats in the opening round, although East Germany had to stave off a strong challenge from the Bulgarians, bronze medalists at the last World Championships. In the final, East Germany won the gold medal handily, but a surprise came in the race for second place, when China won its first Olympic rowing medal ever by taking silver well ahead of the third-place Romanians. The Chinese women also took bronze in Seoul in the coxed eights event, while the entire Romanian crew later helped their nation win silver in the same event."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "East Germany"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/37568"} "Martina Walther"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/37528"} "Gerlinde Doberschütz"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/37535"} "Carola Hornig"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/37731"} "Birte Siech"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/37550"} "Sylvia Rose"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "People's Republic of China"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/36350"} "Zhang Xianghua"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/36333"} "Hu Yadong"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/36348"} "Yang Xiao"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/36353"} "Zhou Shouying"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/36337"} "Li Ronghua"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}